# AUD-CORE (UE FActiveSound + USoundWave loading): every voice opens its clip through miniaudio's resource manager
# over the engine FileSystem (job thread, not the game thread), plays in the class and with the loading its
# `.desound` states (SNDW v1: Class, Loading), and a spatial emitter sounds from its WORLD position.
# Before the run: scripts/Dev/migrate.sh --write over Mirage (every SNDW v0 `.desound` -> v1, Class Effects,
# Loading Resident) - the editor refuses a v0 sound by name ("SNDW v0 states no Class and no Loading").
# Sound is not a picture: the proof is the editor log the player keeps beside the frames (scn-latest/editor.log).
Проект ../Mirage/Mirage.deproj
Дано run Scene "Open Scene MainMenu.desce"
Дано run Action "Play from Here"
Дано advance 1
# Тогда [7a_audio_play]: the menu in Play; the log holds "[Audio] miniaudio engine initialized (<rate> Hz)" once and
# NO "[Audio] Clip not found", "could not be loaded", "SNDW v0" or "Failed to create a voice" line - every sound the
# menu starts (AudioSource AutoPlay, UI clip Audio tracks) resolved its `.desound` and loaded on the job thread.
Тогда-вид 7a_audio_play the Mirage main menu running in Play, no error toast or log overlay about audio
# A UI click plays a one-shot (Lua Audio.play, Effects, Resident): the pointer onto Credits and a click.
Когда input move - 574,481
Когда input click - left
Когда advance 1
# Тогда [7b_audio_oneshot]: the log still has no "[Audio]" warning or error; a click's one-shot was reclaimed when it
# ended (no growth of voices between two clicks - AUD-DEBUG will show the count; until then the log is the proof).
Тогда-вид 7b_audio_oneshot Credits pressed or its panel open; the editor did not stall on the click (no hitch frame)
# Stop: every voice is released (StopAll moves every slot's generation), Edit mode is silent.
Когда run Action "Stop"
Когда advance 0.5
Тогда-вид 7c_audio_stop the editor back in Edit mode; the log has no "[Audio]" error after Stop
